# Normalise line endings on the way into the repository.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF, so a checkout on Linux produces exactly the
# bytes that are committed and a diff cannot be inflated by line endings. The
# project targets Linux exclusively, so there is no working copy that wants CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide which files are text by looking for NUL bytes, which
# is what keeps the PNGs in `docs/` out of the normalisation without naming them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: normalising these would corrupt them, and the heuristic would
# only get it right by accident.
*.png binary
